+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
+Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 21:57:47 -0500
+Subject: [PATCH] [VideoPlayer] DRM PRIME: composite the GUI into the Dolby
+ Vision signal
+
+The sink decodes every pixel of the Dolby Vision tunnel's frame as its
+packed signal, so the GUI plane over it (the OSD, menus) came out green
+and magenta. While the tunnel is on, CWinSystemGbm::SetGuiCapture has
+the GUI rendered into a texture instead of the GUI plane, which stays
+transparent, and the renderer hands that texture to the engine as its
+overlay, subtitles included, under the OSD as on the GUI plane.
+
+The engine's cost follows the overlay's area, so it gets the areas of
+the controls that drew (CGUIWindowManager::GetRenderedRegions) grouped
+in bands of rows, up to PI_OVERLAY_RECTS (engine API 3): an OSD's top
+and bottom bars rather than the screen between them. During playback a
+change of the GUI waits for the next picture instead of rendering the
+one shown again, and the GUI is drawn at most 12 times a second.
+
+Signed-off-by: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
